### Production Considerations
- **Data Fetching**: Use Promise.all() to avoid waterfalls in server components
- **Caching**: Leverage Next.js automatic caching for static content
- **Security**: Always validate server action inputs with Zod
- **Performance**: Use Suspense boundaries for streaming content
- **Error Handling**: Implement proper error boundaries for server components

### Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- ❌ Client-side data fetching when server components can do it
- ❌ No validation on server action inputs
- ❌ Waterfall data fetching (use Promise.all)
- ❌ Not handling loading states with Suspense
- ❌ Exposing sensitive data in server components

### Quality Gates
- [ ] Server actions validated with Zod
- [ ] Data fetching avoids waterfalls
- [ ] Proper error boundaries implemented
- [ ] Caching strategies applied appropriately
- [ ] Security validation on all inputs
- [ ] Loading states handled with Suspense